      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Objective\n* **LiteLLM Proxy** Using Basic LLM chain, with a proxy for routing to any LLM\n* No code change\n\n* Endpoint: http://host.docker.internal:5678/webhook-test/ng/qna\n\n#### Invocation\n##### WIN:\n```\n Invoke-RestMethod -Uri \"http://host.docker.internal:5678/webhook-test/ng/qna\" -Method POST -ContentType \"application/json\" -Body '{\"userMessage\":\"As a new joiniee how many leaves am I entitled to, in a year?\", \"sessionId\": \"ABC123\"}'\n```\n\n##### Linus/MacOS\ncurl  \"http://host.docker.internal:5678/webhook-test/ng/qna\" -X POST -ContentType \"application/json\" -Body '{\"userMessage\":\"As a new joiniee how many leaves am I entitled to, in a year?\", \"sessionId\": \"ABC123\"}'\n\n\n#### NOTE\n##### Changelog:\n1. Segregated the models (via LiteLLM) of router from the specialized agents, so that we could log the 'route' selectively to LiteLLM for specialized agents\n2. Added 'If' node (checkUserMessage) for handling user request error.\n3. Removed ConversationId passed to Groq LLM as {{  $json.sessionId + ':' + $json.requestId }}, because, Not supported by LLamma (Note recommended)",
